      {
        "id": "p13-q18-explanation",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why if $3^{3x-1}=9$, then $3x-1=2$, so $x=1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Since $9=3^2$ and distinct powers of $3$ have distinct values, $3x-1=2$, giving $x=1$.",
          "worked": "Since $9=3^2$ and the function $3^t$ is strictly increasing, equal powers of $3$ have equal indices.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^{3x-1}&=3^2\\\\3x-1&=2\\\\3x&=3\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q18-equations",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "Similarly, by reducing both sides to powers of the same base, solve:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 3,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p13-q18-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$125^x=\\frac15$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x=-\\frac13$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5^{3x}&=5^{-1}\\\\3x&=-1\\\\x&=-\\frac13\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 34
          },
          {
